# Code Style Rules

- Prefer simple, readable code over clever abstractions.
- Do not create abstractions before there are at least 2 clear use cases.
- Keep functions small and named by intent.
- Avoid deeply nested conditions.
- Prefer early returns.
- Do not leave commented-out code.
- Do not rename existing files/components unless explicitly asked.
- Preserve existing public APIs unless the task requires changing them.
- When changing types, update all affected usages.